==Abstract==
Participate is a simple btx-page uploader tool that should run out of the box
on any php enabled http-server. Users can upload thier home made btx pages.
To ensure that one user can not overwrite the pages of another user you can 
assign every user a numeric range for his pages. The tool does not support
textual page-ids. Only numbers like *2342# are allowed.

==Access configuration==
The access configuration is managed directly in the code through php arrays.
$USER_NUMBER configures how many users you have. Here is an example with 3
users:

$USER_NUMBER = 3;

$USER_NAME[0] = "foo";
$USER_PASS[0] = "bar";
$USER_RANGE_FROM[0] = 23;
$USER_RANGE_TO[0] = 42;

$USER_NAME[1] = "fnord";
$USER_PASS[1] = "dronf";
$USER_RANGE_FROM[1] = 100;
$USER_RANGE_TO[1] = 220;

$USER_NAME[1] = "gabriel";
$USER_PASS[1] = "swordfish";
$USER_RANGE_FROM[1] = 221;
$USER_RANGE_TO[1] = 300;

==Warning==
Do not expect so much about the security of this tool. There is no user login
failure counter or anything that would prevent bruteforce attacks. If your
server is misconfigured it might handout the sourcecode, including all passwords
and usernames. Use it on your own risk and improve it yourself if necessary.


